RSDIS Cooperative Lunar Exploration
Copyright 2026 RSDIS project contributors

This project includes independently authored mission logic, an optional model
download manifest, and adapted energy plugin source from these external projects:

Space ROS demos: https://github.com/space-ros/demos
Space ROS simulation: https://github.com/space-ros/simulation

The upstream lunar demo credits Robin Baran and Stevedan Ogochukwu Omodolor
Omodia. External files remain under their original licences and notices.
The default cooperative prototype uses its own lightweight SDF models. An optional
adapter reuses the upstream rover model with namespaced stock Gazebo joint
controllers. The rsdis_energy_plugins package adapts the upstream rechargeable
battery and solar plugins, preserving their original Apache-2.0 headers. Headers
that credit Alexey Simonov retain that attribution as well. Immutable source
links, source checksums and local modifications are recorded in that package's
UPSTREAM.md and UPSTREAM.json, with a project-wide integration source table in
docs/INTEGRATION_SOURCES.md. Detailed upstream terrain remains a reference asset.

Gazebo system interface details were checked against the public Gazebo Harmonic
documentation and the gz-sim8 source code, licensed by its contributors.
